# Beryl 7 device class-map — snapshot from GL.iNet stock, 2026-08-08
# Pipe-delimited, keyed by MAC (uppercase). Safe to copy onto vanilla OpenWrt
# (e.g. /etc/dashboard/classmap) and read from a shell/ubus dashboard.
#
# Fields: MAC | alias | class | last_known_ip | intended_zone
# Classes mirror gl-client (computer/phone/pad/laptop/television/watch/smartappliances)
# so the dashboard's existing icon logic maps 1:1 with no edits.
#
# Zones: lan=192.168.8.0/24  guest=192.168.9.0/24  iot=192.168.10.0/24
# NOTE: last_known_ip is DHCP-assigned and informational; the router will
# re-lease on vanilla. Keep static leases if you want these IPs preserved.
#
00:11:22:33:44:55|My Laptop|laptop|192.168.8.100|lan
00:11:22:33:44:66|My Phone|phone|192.168.8.101|lan
00:11:22:33:44:77|Smart Plug|smartappliances|192.168.10.50|iot
